# =============================================================================
# Devcontainer environment configuration
# =============================================================================
# Created by initialize.sh on first run, edited via firewall-mode.sh (firewall
# vars) or claude-switch (Claude routing vars). Manual edits are preserved by
# initialize.sh re-runs (idempotent KEY=VALUE updates — comments are NOT
# round-tripped, see below).
#
# Convention : commented vars below are documented defaults — uncomment to
# override. Sections delimit functional scope, ease reading as the file grows.
#
# Note about comments : initialize.sh / set_env_var() only edit `KEY=VALUE`
# lines (idempotent replace or append). Inline comments and section headers
# are preserved on existing lines but not propagated to lines initialize.sh
# appends. Keep this template tidy and copy fresh sections in by hand when
# the structure evolves.
# =============================================================================


# === Project & volumes =======================================================

# Unique per workspace folder — used for volume names (optional).
# Change if you have multiple checkouts to keep sessions separate.
# Default : dc-project
#DC_PROJECT={{PROJECT_ID}}

# Share Claude credentials across devcontainers (optional).
# Set the same volume name in all projects to share credentials.
# The volume must exist (created manually or by another project).
#CLAUDE_CREDS_VOLUME=claude-creds-shared


# === System ==================================================================

# Timezone (default : Europe/Paris)
#TZ=Europe/Paris


# === Notify daemon ===========================================================
# Host-side desktop notification daemon. It ships inside
# @meitogi/devcontainer-cli and runs from there — the tree keeps no copy,
# so a `devc` bump moves every project onto the same build at once.

# Channels à activer : `all` (défaut) ou liste CSV parmi toast,sound,flash,discord.
# - toast    : OS-native notification (system tray / Notification Center)
# - sound    : audio cue (système ou fichier custom via NOTIFY_SOUND)
# - flash    : flash de la fenêtre VS Code (Windows uniquement, no-op ailleurs)
# - discord  : webhook Discord (requiert NOTIFY_DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL)
#NOTIFY_CHANNELS=all

# Son joué par le channel `sound`. Par défaut = son OS-natif.
# - `default`  : son système (Glass.aiff macOS / Asterisk Windows / freedesktop Linux)
# - `/abs/path/to/file.wav` : fichier custom (WAV cross-OS ; AIFF/MP3 OK macOS, OGG OK Linux)
# - `off`      : désactive le sound channel même s'il est dans NOTIFY_CHANNELS
#NOTIFY_SOUND=default

# Webhook Discord pour le channel `discord`. Requis si discord est demandé.
# Le token est redacté dans tous les logs / readback (****<last4> visible pour debug).
#NOTIFY_DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL=https://discord.com/api/webhooks/.../...

# TTL des *.jsonl en queue (défaut 24 h). parseFloat → fractions OK (`0.5` = 30 min).
#NOTIFY_CLEANUP_MAX_AGE_HOURS=24

# Répertoire du daemon, si vous en faites tourner une autre copie que celle
# embarquée dans le CLI — développement du daemon, ou correctif local en
# attendant une release. Chemin absolu, ou relatif à .devcontainer/.
# Absent = la copie du paquet, et c'est ce que vous voulez.
#NOTIFY_DAEMON_DIR=


# === scan-deps ===============================================================
# SessionStart hook (.devcontainer/skills/scan-deps/scan-deps-suggest-stale.sh)
# injects a banner when project manifests are newer than firewall/domains.d/<eco>.txt,
# nudging Claude to propose /scan-deps. Uncomment to silence the nudge for the
# whole session — the /scan-deps skill remains invokable on demand.
#SCAN_DEPS_HOOK_DISABLED=1


# === Firewall ================================================================
# Mode source of truth = /workspace/.devcontainer/.configured-firewall-mode
#   off     = no filter (direct internet, emergency kill-switch)
#   basic   = DNS allowlist only
#   strict  = DNS + mitmproxy force-proxy + path-scope enforcement addons (the default)
# To flip mode without touching the flag file by hand :
#   .devcontainer/firewall-mode.sh <off|basic|strict>
# (edits the flag + .env, then rebuild the container). Legacy aliases `okeish`
# and `paranoid` are still accepted with a deprecated-alias warning.

# Network access : host:port pairs (comma-separated, default : none).
#   "host" = Docker host gateway, anything else = DNS (container name).
#   Examples : my-db:3306,host:11434 / mysql:3306 / host:11434
# Rebuild after editing — iptables rules apply at container boot.
#CLAUDE_CODE_FIREWALL_ALLOWED=

# Verbose firewall logging.
#CLAUDE_CODE_FIREWALL_DEBUG=true

# Bake firewall/domains.local.txt + firewall/policy.local.d/ into the image ?
#   0 (default) = no. The build ships only committed sources ; your local
#                 overrides are applied per-container, on demand, by a human :
#                     wtf firewall reload        (from a host terminal)
#                 Preview the diff first, unprivileged :
#                     reload-firewall --dry-run
#   1           = yes. Convenience : overrides survive rebuilds, no reload.
#
# Why 0 by default : those two paths are gitignored and writable by anything
# running in the container. At 1, "an npm postinstall appended a domain" and
# "you rebuilt the container" combine into a wider firewall that nothing
# flagged. At 0 a human sees the diff before it takes effect.
#
# Personal setting. Leave it out of devcontainer.json — a team default of 1
# would silently harden nobody. The build log always states which mode ran and
# how many hosts the choice costs.
#FIREWALL_ALLOW_LOCAL_AT_REBUILD=1


# === Local Ollama / Local Claude bridge sidecar ==============================
# (cf. /opt/devcontainer/base/knowledge/ollama-local.md — "Mode local-proxy" section)
#
# Three modes coexist, toggleable from the HOST via :
#   bash .devcontainer/host-helpers/claude-switch {local|local-proxy|cloud|status}
# Then Rebuild Container in VSCode so docker-compose re-reads .env at
# container creation (Reload Window is NOT enough — PID 1 freezes env at
# boot ; cf. claude-switch's own messages).
#
# CLAUDE_CODE_FIREWALL_ALLOWED opens iptables ACCEPT for :
#   host:11434         — direct Ollama on the Mac host
#   claude-bridge:9223 — UniClaudeProxy sidecar : translates reasoning
#                        models' <think> blocks into Claude Code's
#                        expected format. Requires the sidecar to be
#                        running — see /opt/devcontainer/base/knowledge/ollama-local.md.
# Keep both listed → flip local ↔ local-proxy without a firewall rebuild.
#CLAUDE_CODE_FIREWALL_ALLOWED=host:11434,claude-bridge:9223

# --- Audited Anthropic base URLs (exactly ONE active at a time) --------------
# claude-switch toggles the comment prefix on the line matching the chosen
# mode. The other audited URL stays commented. `cloud` mode comments both
# audited lines so Claude Code falls back to api.anthropic.com.

# Mode `local` : direct Ollama, raw — no thinking translation.
# ⚠ Reasoning models (qwen3, deepseek-r1) will hang Claude Code on the
#   raw <think> blocks Ollama 0.24 surfaces verbatim. Use `local-proxy`
#   for those.
#ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=http://ollama.internal:11434

# Mode `local-proxy` : via UniClaudeProxy sidecar (translates <think>
# blocks → Anthropic-spec `thinking` content blocks). Recommended default
# for reasoning models. Audited path through mitm (policy.d/claude-bridge.yaml,
# STRICT 1:1 mirror of api.anthropic.com.yaml on /v1/messages).
#ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=http://claude-bridge:9223

# Bypass (debug only) : same sidecar but skips mitm. Useful to isolate
# streaming bugs, measure raw latency, or as a kill-switch when policy
# enforcement misbehaves. NEVER touched by claude-switch — manual edit,
# same ergonomics as `ollama.local` for the direct Ollama path.
#ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=http://claude-bridge.local:9223

# --- Shared across ALL local modes (ignored in cloud) ------------------------
#ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=ollama

# Isolate Claude Code state (credentials, session history, todos) for local
# modes. ~/.claude-local is initialized by post-start.sh when this var is
# active in .env at container boot — with skills/commands/memory/plugins/
# settings.json/.claude.json symlinked from ~/.claude so updates to skills +
# hooks + memory propagate to both modes. Cloud OAuth creds in
# ~/.claude/.credentials.json are NEVER touched by local mode — guarantees
# no contamination of the shared CLAUDE_CREDS_VOLUME.
#CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=/home/node/.claude-local

# Force a single model name for BOTH main and small-fast Claude Code calls, so
# Ollama only ever loads ONE model into RAM (vs main=opus + small=haiku, which
# would allocate two distinct slots). Setting both to claude-opus-4-7 makes
# local mode transparent in the UI — Claude Code displays "opus" while routing
# to whatever model you aliased with `ollama cp <your-model> claude-opus-4-7`
# on the host. Critical on 16 GB Macs — pairs with OLLAMA_MAX_LOADED_MODELS=1
# in the `ollama-serve-16k` host helper. UniClaudeProxy then re-routes the
# `claude-opus-4-7` request name to Ollama via config.json model mapping.
#ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-4-7
#ANTHROPIC_SMALL_FAST_MODEL=claude-opus-4-7

# Lifecycle hook xtrace — when DEBUG=1, initialize.sh / on-create.sh /
# post-create.sh / post-start.sh write a per-hook .trace file in
# .devcontainer/tmp/logs/ (every executed shell command with file:line). Useful
# when a hook crashes and you need to know exactly which line — tail
# .devcontainer/tmp/logs/<hook>-<latest>.trace. Off by default to keep logs lean.
#DEBUG=1

# --- Base image (published on GHCR) -----------------------------------------
# The project Dockerfile FROMs this tag; compose pulls it, nothing is built
# locally. Tag scheme: <base-version>-cc<claude-code-version> — the pairs
# published together are listed in the devcontainer-sandbox repo's
# cc-versions.json. Unset = the default in docker-compose.yml.
# The three published lines: 1.5.0-cc2.1.280 (default), 1.5.0-cc2.1.272,
# 1.5.0-cc2.1.220.
#BASE_IMAGE=ghcr.io/meitogi/devcontainer-sandbox:1.5.0-cc2.1.280
# --- VS Code extension patches ---------------------------------------------
# The image installs the Claude Code extension exactly as published and patches
# nothing by itself. The 45-ext-patches.sh hook applies YOUR patchers to your
# copy at container create, and re-checks at every start — from a repository
# (EXT_PATCHES_REPO + EXT_PATCHES_TOKEN, a GitHub fine-grained PAT, read-only,
# Contents: read, on that one repository), or from a directory that already
# holds the .py patchers (EXT_PATCHES_DIR: a bind mount or a shared named
# volume — no network, no token). `<change-me>` is a placeholder, not a token:
# with it in place the hook applies nothing and says so; `devc initialize`
# replaces it from ~/.config/devc/ext-patches.env when that file exists.
EXT_PATCHES_REPO=meitogi/claude-ext-patchs
EXT_PATCHES_TOKEN=<change-me>
#EXT_PATCHES_DIR=/opt/ext-patchs
#
# Which set: unset = auto — the newest tag cut for the Claude Code version this
# container runs (cc<version>-r<n>), resolved from the cache first, then from
# the repository's tags, never HEAD. A boot never moves on its own; in the
# container, `ext-patches-update` moves to a newer -r deliberately. Pin a tag
# or a commit SHA here only to freeze a set:
#EXT_PATCHES_REF=cc2.1.280-r1
#
# A version with no tag of its own is refused rather than served another
# version's set; this takes the repository's HEAD instead, pinned back as the
# commit it resolved to (ext-patches-update writes it).
#EXT_PATCHES_ALLOW_UNTESTED=1
#
# Which of them to apply: all, none, a category (ux, fix, notify) or a
# comma-separated list of categories and names. Defaults to all.
#EXT_PATCHES_SELECT=all
